01:02:48.530 --> 01:02:51.520
And I wanted to show you an example of
where we've done that.

01:02:51.520 --> 01:02:53.380
And that is with Facebook photos.

01:02:53.380 --> 01:02:55.510
We have billions of users and rated photos

01:02:55.510 --> 01:02:58.340
from people all around the world on
Facebook.

01:02:58.340 --> 01:03:00.920
And we can force people all around the
world to

01:03:00.920 --> 01:03:05.060
always enter the caption or an on text for
their photo.

01:03:05.060 --> 01:03:09.030
So to solve this problem we built
something called the caption generator.

01:03:09.030 --> 01:03:11.590
The caption generator takes bits of
metadata

01:03:11.590 --> 01:03:14.030
associated with the photo, who uploaded
the

01:03:14.030 --> 01:03:17.800
photo, where was the photo uploaded, who
are the people tagged in the photo.

01:03:17.800 --> 01:03:20.180
And it generates a caption or an alt text

01:03:20.180 --> 01:03:23.100
for the image, which we then associate
with the image.

01:03:23.100 --> 01:03:25.590
So when, when someone lands on the photo

01:03:25.590 --> 01:03:27.930
it, it announces this nice caption for the
photo.

